<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content="Annotated box model of a real element.">
  <meta name="author" content="Pranav Arora">
  <title>Box Model – Annotated</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
      max-width: 860px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
    /* THE ELEMENT BEING ANALYSED */
    .my-box {
      width: 200px;
      height: 80px;
      padding: 20px;
      border: 10px solid #1d3557;
      margin: 30px;
      background: #a8dadc;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      font-weight: bold;
    }
    /* VISUAL LAYERS */
    .layer {
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      position: relative;
      text-align: center;
      font-size: .8rem;
    }
    .l-margin {
      background: #f9cb9c;
      padding: 36px;
    }
    .l-border {
      background: #ffe599;
      padding: 22px;
    }
    .l-padding {
      background: #b6d7a8;
      padding: 36px;
    }
    .l-content {
      background: #9fc5e8;
      padding: 28px 40px;
    }
    .tag {
      position: absolute;
      top: 3px;
      left: 8px;
      font-weight: bold;
    }
    .demo {
      display: flex;
      gap: 2rem;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
    table {
      border-collapse: collapse;
    }
    th,
    td {
      border: 1px solid #999;
      padding: .35rem .7rem;
    }
    code {
      background: #eee;
      padding: 0 .25rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Box Model of <code>.my-box</code></h1>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="my-box">Hello</div>
    <!-- Annotated diagram -->
    <div class="layer l-margin">
      <span class="tag">margin 30px</span>
      <div class="layer l-border">
        <span class="tag">border 10px</span>
        <div class="layer l-padding">
          <span class="tag">padding 20px</span>
          <div class="layer l-content">
            content<br>200 × 80
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <h2>Calculation (default box-sizing: content-box)</h2>
  <table>
    <tr>
      <th>Total width</th>
      <td>200 + (20 × 2) + (10 × 2) = <strong>260px</strong>
        (+60px margin = 320px)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Total height</th>
      <td>80 + (20 × 2) + (10 × 2) = <strong>140px</strong>
        (+60px margin = 200px)</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  <h2>With box-sizing: border-box</h2>
  <p>
    The same width of 200px would include padding and border.
    The box stays 200px wide and the content shrinks to 140px.
    This is why developers often use:
  </p>
  <p><code>* { box-sizing: border-box; }</code></p>
  <p>
    <strong>Tip:</strong> Open DevTools using F12 → Elements →
    Computed tab to inspect the box model of an element.
  </p>
  <footer>
    <p>Created by Pranav Arora | BCA Artificial Intelligence</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
